From 328cbea93a3eee0bf47f3563a27a14f4734c000b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michaelkremenetsky
 <28833521+michaelkremenetsky@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 10:28:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/20] next: build non-inline const rcstr! statics at runtime
 (LazyLock) on wasm

A non-inline (>7 char) rcstr! literal can't be a `const RcStr` on 16/32-bit
targets (wasm32): turbo-rcstr's tagged value stores the interned static's
pointer as an integer, and const-eval rejects pointer-to-integer casts
("unable to turn pointer into integer"). Convert those module-level constants
to runtime `static X: LazyLock<RcStr>` and deref at the use sites.

Covers SOURCE_URL_PROTOCOL (turbopack-core) and its downstream uses
(turbopack-css, next-api, next-napi-bindings), USER_AGENT_FOR_GOOGLE_FONTS and
GOOGLE_FONTS_INTERNAL_PREFIX (next-core), and the babel loader/react-compiler
constants. PROJECT_FILESYSTEM_NAME stays a const (its "project" literal is
inline, so it const-evals). LazyLock is unconditional (not cfg'd on wasm) so
the change is target-agnostic and native builds are unaffected.
